<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-21T00:02:52+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:02:52 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Two Andaman, one Chhattisgarh site added to Unesco World Heritage tentative list]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-andaman-one-chhattisgarh-site-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-tentative-list/articleshow/135075402.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135075402.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India has added three sites to its tentative list for UNESCO World Heritage status, including the Karst-mud-volcano Complex. The sites are located in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands and Chhattisgarh, and the Archaeological Survey of India played a crucial role. Inclusion on this list is necessary for future nominations to the UNESCO World Heritage List. Currently, India possesses 45 UNESCO World Heritage Sites, ranking sixth in the world.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-andaman-one-chhattisgarh-site-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-tentative-list/articleshow/135075402.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-andaman-one-chhattisgarh-site-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-tentative-list/articleshow/135075402.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T23:59:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135075477,imgsize-321930.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shinde calls INDIA bloc ‘ten-headed Ravana’, accuses Uddhav of ‘vote theft’]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shinde-calls-india-bloc-ten-headed-ravana-accuses-uddhav-of-vote-theft/articleshow/135074840.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135074840.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shinde-calls-india-bloc-ten-headed-ravana-accuses-uddhav-of-vote-theft/articleshow/135074840.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shinde-calls-india-bloc-ten-headed-ravana-accuses-uddhav-of-vote-theft/articleshow/135074840.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T23:22:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135074893,imgsize-73330.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi BJP leader burns giant cockroach effigy; CJP founder responds with SRK’s 'Swades' song]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/free-publicity-cjp-reacts-as-delhi-burns-30ft-cockroach-effigy-with-ravan/articleshow/135073600.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135073600.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During Dussehra celebrations in Delhi, a 30-foot cockroach effigy was burned alongside traditional effigies of Ravan. Organizers stated that the effigy symbolized filth and promoted cleanliness in line with health awareness initiatives. Leaders of the Cockroach Janta Party reacted sharply, suggesting the move provided them with free publicity. Delhi minister Kapil Mishra remarked that cockroaches symbolize chaos and filth, reflecting public sentiment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/free-publicity-cjp-reacts-as-delhi-burns-30ft-cockroach-effigy-with-ravan/articleshow/135073600.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/free-publicity-cjp-reacts-as-delhi-burns-30ft-cockroach-effigy-with-ravan/articleshow/135073600.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T22:15:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135073750,imgsize-68136.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[No double standards on terror, need unified action to dismantle its entire ecosystem: Rajnath at SCO]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-double-standards-on-terror-need-unified-action-to-dismantle-its-entire-ecosystem-rajnath-at-sco/articleshow/135073553.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135073553.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-double-standards-on-terror-need-unified-action-to-dismantle-its-entire-ecosystem-rajnath-at-sco/articleshow/135073553.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-double-standards-on-terror-need-unified-action-to-dismantle-its-entire-ecosystem-rajnath-at-sco/articleshow/135073553.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T22:04:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135073683,imgsize-127128.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Expect partners to show zero tolerance on terrorism': EAM thanks US for handing over Tahawwur Rana]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/expect-partners-to-show-zero-tolerance-on-terrorism-eam-thanks-us-for-handing-over-tahawwur-rana/articleshow/135072738.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135072738.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/expect-partners-to-show-zero-tolerance-on-terrorism-eam-thanks-us-for-handing-over-tahawwur-rana/articleshow/135072738.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/expect-partners-to-show-zero-tolerance-on-terrorism-eam-thanks-us-for-handing-over-tahawwur-rana/articleshow/135072738.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T21:08:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135072878,imgsize-115076.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Youth on streets are revolutionaries': Uddhav Thackeray calls for 'regime change']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/youth-on-streets-are-revolutionaries-uddhav-thackeray-calls-for-regime-change/articleshow/135072727.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135072727.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During the vibrant Dussehra rally at Shivaji Park in Mumbai, Uddhav Thackeray rallied his supporters, highlighting the significance of youth activism in addressing the alleged electoral irregularities impacting the fresh electorate. He proclaimed that the saffron identity is a legacy of his party, urging a reformation in the political climate and the prominent display of the saffron flag, echoing the influence of Bal Thackeray in his passionate address.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/youth-on-streets-are-revolutionaries-uddhav-thackeray-calls-for-regime-change/articleshow/135072727.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/youth-on-streets-are-revolutionaries-uddhav-thackeray-calls-for-regime-change/articleshow/135072727.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T21:05:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135072783,imgsize-151444.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Identify, defeat forces against India: Modi calls for unity, self-reliance]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/identify-defeat-forces-against-india-modi-calls-for-unity-self-reliance/articleshow/135072362.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135072362.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[PM urges parties, institutions to put nation first; says national self-respect and strength key to overcoming challenges]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/identify-defeat-forces-against-india-modi-calls-for-unity-self-reliance/articleshow/135072362.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/identify-defeat-forces-against-india-modi-calls-for-unity-self-reliance/articleshow/135072362.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T20:35:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135072362,imgsize-86758.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[PM Modi invokes 'Ram Rajya', warns against people hurting India's image - top quotes from Dussehra event]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-invokes-ram-rajya-warns-against-people-hurting-indias-image-top-quotes-from-dussehra-event/articleshow/135071521.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135071521.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi addressed the Dussehra celebrations and highlighted the importance of public welfare. He emphasized the need for social justice and self-reliance as central to national development. Modi reminded attendees of the ideals of Lord Ram, focusing on justice and equal opportunities. He encouraged recognizing India's potential while serving the poor and marginalized. The Prime Minister referenced Vijayadashami as a celebration of the triumph of good over evil.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-invokes-ram-rajya-warns-against-people-hurting-indias-image-top-quotes-from-dussehra-event/articleshow/135071521.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-invokes-ram-rajya-warns-against-people-hurting-indias-image-top-quotes-from-dussehra-event/articleshow/135071521.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T19:28:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071579,imgsize-225102.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: Rubio calls India a refining superpower; Kharge to raise SIR, delimitation concerns with PM Modi &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rubio-calls-india-a-refining-superpower-kharge-to-raise-sir-delimitation-concerns-with-pm-modi-more/articleshow/135070304.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135070304.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rubio-calls-india-a-refining-superpower-kharge-to-raise-sir-delimitation-concerns-with-pm-modi-more/articleshow/135070304.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rubio-calls-india-a-refining-superpower-kharge-to-raise-sir-delimitation-concerns-with-pm-modi-more/articleshow/135070304.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:51:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071003,imgsize-1865722.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Doing a real disservice’: Annamalai backs CJP leaders, questions their continued custody]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doing-a-real-disservice-annamalai-backs-cjp-leaders-questions-their-continued-custody/articleshow/135070878.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135070878.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doing-a-real-disservice-annamalai-backs-cjp-leaders-questions-their-continued-custody/articleshow/135070878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doing-a-real-disservice-annamalai-backs-cjp-leaders-questions-their-continued-custody/articleshow/135070878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:47:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070912,imgsize-1120106.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Air India Express flight suffers bird strike, lands safely in Bengaluru]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-express-flight-suffers-bird-strike-lands-safely-in-bengaluru/articleshow/135070745.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135070745.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[An Air India Express flight en route from Bhogapuram to Bengaluru encountered a bird strike on Monday, yet all 148 passengers and crew emerged safely. Following the event, technical teams diligently inspected the aircraft, confirming it was in good condition for future flights. Notably, a comparable bird strike event affected an Emirates flight just days earlier on October 17.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-express-flight-suffers-bird-strike-lands-safely-in-bengaluru/articleshow/135070745.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-express-flight-suffers-bird-strike-lands-safely-in-bengaluru/articleshow/135070745.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:43:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070840,imgsize-61370.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amit Shah meets families of anti-drug campaigners killed in Punjab; targets AAP on open drug trade]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135069001.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amit Shah visited families of drug-related victims in Punjab, expressing condolences and discussing safety issues. He criticised the AAP government for its failure to tackle the drug menace effectively. Shah highlighted the dangers faced by those who oppose drug trafficking in the state. The recent murder of anti-drug activist Parvinder Singh Jhota escalated political tensions in Punjab.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T17:07:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135069053,imgsize-1436186.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Felt very happy’: Annamalai welcomes Bhagwat's remarks on Muslims' place in India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/felt-very-happy-annamalai-welcomes-bhagwats-remarks-on-muslims-place-in-india/articleshow/135068592.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135068592.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[K Annamalai lauded Mohan Bhagwat's recent statements on the significance of religious inclusivity in India. Speaking at a Faith Leaders Conference in New York, Bhagwat encouraged the embrace of diverse communities, including Muslims, reiterating the value of dignity for all. Annamalai pointed out the rising global fascination with Indian civilization, stressing the necessity for leaders and citizens to embody the nation's established ideals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/felt-very-happy-annamalai-welcomes-bhagwats-remarks-on-muslims-place-in-india/articleshow/1350685